	"result": "learn: Both commits that add the dogfood README sit in a gitignored `reports/` folder and were force-added, so later edits to those files won't show up in `git status`.\ntag: Heads up\nexplain:\n**Force-added files in ignored folders**\n- `reports/` is listed in .gitignore, so the main agent used `git add -f` to commit the dogfood README on `feat/2.1.327-next` and on `side`.\n- Git tracks a force-added file normally from then on, so edits to those two README files will show up in `git status`.\n- Any new file you create under `reports/` stays ignored and will not show up in `git status`, so it can be missed in a commit.\n- The `side` branch adds the same path with different content, so merging it conflicts (add/add).\n- Check `git ls-files reports/` to see what is actually tracked, and decide whether `reports/` should stay ignored.",
